Or when you want to have the "trouble" - once and install time or
everytime you want to decode something.

Trouble to install Mnenhy:
Go to its homepage. Download it. Install it.

Trouble to install rot13.com:
None, obviously.

Trouble to use Mnenhy:
Mark the text (actually you don't have to do that, if you want the whole
post decoded), right click, decode->rot13

Trouble to use rot13.com:
Mark the text, right click, copy text, open web browser, wait for it to
start ;-), go to rot13.com, right click, paste text

Given that you only have to go through the (trivial) install process
once, I'd say, when you're planning on decoding rot13 regularly, you
save more time using Mnenhy than not.


